This got pasted with weird leading indentation and two loose functions. Clean it up and group `fizzbuzz` and `countdown` as static methods on a `Sequences` object. Code:

```jac
    def fizzbuzz(n: int) -> str {
        if n % 15 == 0 { return "FizzBuzz"; }
        elif n % 3 == 0 { return "Fizz"; }
        elif n % 5 == 0 { return "Buzz"; }
        return str(n);
    }

    def countdown(n: int) -> Generator[int] {
        while n > 0 {
            yield n;
            n -= 1;
        }
    }

    with entry {
        results = [fizzbuzz(i) for i in range(1, 16)];
        print(results);
        print([x for x in countdown(5)]);
    }
```

Before I move `countdown` -- it's a generator (`yield`). Wrapping a generator as a `static def` on an obj is fine in Jac, the `-> Generator[int]` return type carries over unchanged. I'll fix the indentation too. Callers become `Sequences.fizzbuzz(...)` and `Sequences.countdown(...)`:

```jac
obj Sequences {
    static def fizzbuzz(n: int) -> str {
        if n % 15 == 0 { return "FizzBuzz"; }
        elif n % 3 == 0 { return "Fizz"; }
        elif n % 5 == 0 { return "Buzz"; }
        return str(n);
    }
    static def countdown(n: int) -> Generator[int] {
