Backend walkers are fine. In the frontend `app`, the mount handler has a real bug that's inconsistent with the rest of your code:

```jac
if result.reports {
    tasks = result.reports;
}
```

`get_tasks` does `report [-->][?:Task]` — a single report whose value is the *list* of tasks. So `result.reports` is `[[task, task, ...]]` — a one-element array containing your list. Assigning that to `tasks` means you're iterating over a list-of-one-list, and `{t.title}` on the inner list won't work. Note your own `toggle` handler correctly uses `result.reports[0]`. The loader should too.

